{"book":16,"chapter":2,"rubric":"FROM ASSEMBLER TO C / LANGUAGE BASICS / CHAPTER 2","slides":[{"title":"Labels and jumps","sub":"Chapter 2 · Structure and assembler","short":"Intro","main":"C's structured constructs are the same labels and jumps.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["In assembler","In C","The same thing"],"captions":["Assembler has no if or while: just labels and conditional jumps, which you wrote in Mini-8 and RISC-V","C writes the same jumps in a structured way: if, while, for, switch","The compiler turns the structure back into labels and jumps, so you can always picture the result"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":100.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["      li   a5, 0",".L1:  bge  a5, a0, .L2","      addi a5, a5, 1","      j    .L1",".L2:"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"asm","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":200.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":100.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {","    ...","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":200.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":12.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["while (i < n) {","    i++;","}"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":130.0},{"t":"code","id":"a","x":170.0,"y":38.0,"lines":[".L1: bge a5,a0,.L2","     addi a5,a5,1","     j .L1",".L2:"],"lang":"asm","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":180.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"loop = label + check + jump back","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.5,28.3]}]},{"title":"if and else","sub":"Compare and branch","short":"if","main":"Always use curly braces: that's how the goto fail bug appeared.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Condition","else","Always braces"],"captions":["if turns into a compare and branch: if the condition is false, jump over the body","else is one more unconditional jump over the second branch; else if chains are a sequence of checks","Without curly braces the \"second line\" always runs: that's the famous goto fail bug"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["if (x > 0) {","    y = 1;","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":140.0},{"t":"code","id":"a","x":170.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["ble  a0, zero, .L1","li   a1, 1",".L1:"],"hl":[0],"lang":"asm","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":180.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["if (x > 0) {","    y = 1;","} else {","    y = -1;","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":16.0,"w":140.0},{"t":"code","id":"a","x":170.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["ble  a0, zero, .L1","li   a1, 1","j    .L2",".L1: li a1, -1",".L2:"],"hl":[2],"lang":"asm","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":190.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["if (err)","    goto fail;","    goto fail;   // always!","ok();"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"an extra line without braces: the check is disabled","tone":"red","size":9.5}]],"cues":[13.0,24.4]}]},{"title":"switch","sub":"Jump table","short":"switch","main":"Without break, execution falls through into the next branch.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["switch","Jump table","Fall-through"],"captions":["switch picks a branch by an integer value; each branch ends with break","If the values are dense, the compiler builds an array of addresses and makes one indirect jump by index","Without break, execution falls through into the next branch: useful for merging cases, but more often a bug"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["switch (op) {","case '+': r = a + b; break;","case '-': r = a - b; break;","default: r = 0;","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"i","x":60.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"op - '+'","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":190.0,"y":40.0,"w":90.0,"h":24.0,"text":"+ → L1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":190.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":24.0,"text":"- → L2","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":190.0,"y":100.0,"w":90.0,"h":24.0,"text":"× → L3","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":96.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":142.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":190.0,"y":140.0,"text":"jr via address table","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["case 1:","    puts(\"one\");","case 2:            // no break!","    puts(\"two\");","    break;"],"hl":[2,3],"bad":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"x == 1 prints both one and two","tone":"red","size":9.5}]],"cues":[15.1,31.9]}]},{"title":"Loops","sub":"while, do-while, for","short":"Loops","main":"A loop = label, check, body, step and a jump back.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["while and do-while","for","break and continue"],"captions":["while checks the condition at the start, do-while at the end, so the body runs at least once","for gathers init, condition and step in one line; a variable declared in the header is visible only in the loop","break leaves the loop, continue goes to the next iteration: both are just jumps to labels"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":12.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["while (i < n) {","    ...","}","","do {","    ...","} while (i < n);"],"hl":[0,6],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":15.0,"w":150.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"check → body","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"body → check","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {","    sum += a[i];","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"init; while (cond) { body; step; }","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {","    if (a[i] < 0) continue;","    if (a[i] == x) break;","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"continue → step, break → after the loop","size":9.5}]],"cues":[15.7,26.5]}]},{"title":"Functions","sub":"Prototypes and parameters","short":"Functions","main":"Parameters are passed by value; f(void) means no arguments.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Prototype and definition","Parameters by value","void and empty parentheses"],"captions":["Before a call the compiler must know the signature: declare a prototype, and the definition may be lower or in another file","A copy of the value goes into the function: changing the parameter doesn't affect the caller's variable","f(void) means \"no parameters\"; f() in the old syntax means \"anything\": always write void"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["int sum(int a, int b);        // prototype","","int main(void) { return sum(1, 2); }","","int sum(int a, int b) { return a + b; }"],"hl":[0,4],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["void f(int x) { x = 99; }","int n = 5;","f(n);","// n is still 5"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":180.0},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":60.0,"h":34.0,"text":"n\n5","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":270.0,"y":110.0,"w":60.0,"h":34.0,"text":"x (copy)\n99","tone":"yellow","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["int f(void);   // no parameters","int g();       // any arguments!"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"text","id":"n~text","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"in C23 g() also means void","tone":"yellow","size":9.0}]],"cues":[15.4,30.5]}]},{"title":"Call and stack","sub":"a0…a7, ra, frame","short":"Call","main":"Arguments in registers, return address in ra, frame on the stack, result in a0.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Arguments in a0…a7","Frame and ra","Return"],"captions":["The caller puts arguments in registers a0, a1, … and runs jal: the address of the next instruction is saved in ra","The called function moves sp down, creates a frame, and saves ra and the needed s-registers in it","The result is in a0; the function restores registers, returns sp and runs ret: a jump via ra"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["li   a0, 3","li   a1, 4","jal  ra, sum","# a0 = result"],"hl":[2],"lang":"asm","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":150.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":270.0,"y":40.0,"w":90.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a0 = 3","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a1 = 4","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"ra","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":90.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ra = return","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":100.0,"y":40.0,"w":170.0,"h":38.0,"text":"","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"mt","x":100.0,"y":29.0,"text":"main","tone":"green","size":8.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"mv0","x":100.0,"y":41.0,"text":"locals","size":8.5,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"mv1","x":100.0,"y":53.0,"text":"...","size":8.5,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":100.0,"y":98.0,"w":170.0,"h":51.0,"text":"","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"ft","x":100.0,"y":80.5,"text":"sum","tone":"green","size":8.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"fv0","x":100.0,"y":92.5,"text":"ra (saved)","size":8.5,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"fv1","x":100.0,"y":104.5,"text":"s0","size":8.5,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"fv2","x":100.0,"y":116.5,"text":"locals","size":8.5,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"sp","x":250.0,"y":100.0,"text":"◀ sp","tone":"green","size":10.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":60.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["add  a0, a0, a1","ld   ra, 8(sp)","addi sp, sp, 16","ret"],"hl":[3],"lang":"asm","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":220.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"ret = jump to the address in ra","size":9.5}]],"cues":[12.1,27.2]}]},{"title":"Scope and lifetime","sub":"Locals, static","short":"Scope","main":"Locals die with their frame; never return the address of a local.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Local","static","Address of a local"],"captions":["A local is visible in its block and lives while the block runs: after exit its stack slot is taken by someone else's frame","static extends lifetime: the variable lives in .data/.bss and keeps its value between calls; on a global, static limits visibility to the file","You can't return the address of a local: the frame is gone, and the pointer looks into someone else's memory"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["void f(void) {","    int a = 1;","    {","        int b = 2;","    }   // b died","}   // a died"],"hl":[4,5],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":16.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int counter(void) {","    static int n = 0;","    return ++n;","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":260.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":310.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":40.0,"text":".data\nn: 0→1→2","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int *f(void) {","    int a = 5;","    return &a;   // ✕","}"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":260.0},{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":310.0,"y":76.0,"w":90.0,"h":46.0,"text":"warning:\nfunction returns\naddress of local","tone":"yellow","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.4,26.4]}]},{"title":"Recursion","sub":"Frames and tail call","short":"Recursion","main":"Depth is limited by the stack; a tail call depends on optimization.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Factorial","Frames pile up","Tail recursion"],"captions":["A recursive function calls itself, and each call gets its own frame on the stack","Call depth is limited by stack size: infinite recursion ends in a crash","An optimizing compiler replaces a tail call with a jump, but the standard doesn't guarantee it"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int fact(int n) {","    if (n <= 1) return 1;","    return n * fact(n - 1);","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":260.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"f0","x":140.0,"y":30.0,"w":150.0,"h":22.0,"text":"fact(4)","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f1","x":140.0,"y":56.0,"w":150.0,"h":22.0,"text":"fact(3)","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f2","x":140.0,"y":82.0,"w":150.0,"h":22.0,"text":"fact(2)","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f3","x":140.0,"y":108.0,"w":150.0,"h":22.0,"text":"fact(1)","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"s","x":280.0,"y":108.0,"text":"◀ sp","tone":"green","size":10.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":148.0,"text":"4 frames → result 24","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":12.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int sum(int n, int acc) {","    if (n == 0) return acc;","    return sum(n - 1, acc + n);","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":16.0,"w":190.0},{"t":"code","id":"a","x":210.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["# -O2: tail call","addi a0, a0, -1","add  a1, a1, a2","j    sum"],"hl":[3],"lang":"asm","size":8.5,"lh":16.0,"w":150.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"a jump instead of a call: the frame doesn't grow","tone":"green","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.0,33.9]}]},{"title":"Order of evaluation","sub":"Side effects","short":"Order","main":"One variable: at most one change per expression.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Two writes","Sequence points","Rule"],"captions":["An expression that changes one variable twice between sequence points is undefined behavior: i++ + ++i, a[i] = i++","The standard doesn't set the order of evaluating arguments and most operands; guarantees exist for &&, ||, comma, ?: and the end of a full expression","Change a variable at most once per expression and don't pile up side effects"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int i = 1;","int x = i++ + ++i;   // UB","a[i] = i++;           // UB"],"hl":[1,2],"bad":[1,2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"&&   ||","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":", (comma)","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":290.0,"y":56.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"?:","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"text":"after them all side effects have already happened","size":9.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"w":300.0,"h":24.0,"text":"f(a(), b()): the order of calling a and b is not set","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["i++;","x = i + 1;","a[i] = i;","i++;"],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"one effect per expression","tone":"green","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.5,25.1]}]},{"title":"The size_t trap","sub":"Unsigned counters","short":"size_t","main":"i >= 0 is always true for size_t: count down to one or use a signed type.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Infinite loop","Signed and unsigned","Fix"],"captions":["size_t is unsigned: i >= 0 is always true, and 0 - 1 gives the maximum number, so the loop never ends","In a comparison the signed value is converted to unsigned: -1 turns out bigger than any size","Count down to one with index i - 1, use a signed type, or a condition with a postfix decrement"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for (size_t i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {","    use(a[i]);","}"],"hl":[0],"bad":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"i = 0 → i-- → 18446744073709551615","tone":"red","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int a = -1;","size_t n = 5;","if (a < n) ...   // false!"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"-Wsign-compare will warn","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for (size_t i = n; i-- > 0; ) {","    use(a[i]);","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"the condition compares the old value with zero","tone":"green","size":9.5}]],"cues":[18.3,28.4]}]},{"title":"Variable arguments","sub":"stdarg.h","short":"stdarg","main":"The function doesn't know how many arguments of what types it got.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Ellipsis","va_start, va_arg, va_end","Contract"],"captions":["An ellipsis in the parameter list accepts any number of arguments: printf(\"%d %s\", 1, \"x\")","Macros from stdarg.h: va_start remembers the place after the last named parameter, va_arg fetches the next, va_end finishes","The function knows neither the number nor the types of arguments: agree via a format string or a counter; a mistake reads garbage"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["int sum(int n, ...);","","sum(3, 10, 20, 30);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["int sum(int n, ...) {","    va_list ap;","    va_start(ap, n);","    int s = 0;","    while (n--) s += va_arg(ap, int);","    va_end(ap);","    return s;","}"],"hl":[2,4,5],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":15.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["sum(3, 10, 20);   // promised 3, gave 2","printf(\"%d %d\", 1);   // UB"],"hl":[0,1],"bad":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"reads what was never passed","tone":"red","size":9.5}]],"cues":[10.1,31.0]}]},{"title":"Modularity","sub":"static, inline, headers","short":"Modules","main":"Hide details with static, put declarations in headers.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["static functions","inline","Headers"],"captions":["A static function is visible only in its own file: this hides details and gives the compiler the full picture","inline hints to substitute the body instead of a call, avoiding a frame; the compiler makes the final decision","Declarations for other files live in headers with protection against repeated inclusion"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["static int helper(int x) {","    return x * 2;","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":260.0},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":310.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"visible only\nin this .c","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["static inline int sq(int x) {","    return x * x;","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"call sq(a) → mul a0, a0, a0","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#ifndef MATH_H","#define MATH_H","int sum(int a, int b);","#endif"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"protection against double inclusion","size":9.5}]],"cues":[11.9,25.6]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: pointers and arrays.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Correspondences","Traps","What's next"],"captions":["if, switch, loops and calls are labels, jumps and frames; a function's result is in a0","Always braces, break in switch, one side effect per expression, careful with size_t and sign in comparisons","Next: pointers and arrays: addresses you can already read in assembler"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"if / switch → bxx, jr","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"for / while → j back","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":112.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"call → jal, ret","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":270.0,"y":76.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"result in a0","tone":"green","size":9.0,"su